{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-69532",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/2fafbd5822fd6edb578a2ada55a5787cc6f32b301911332115011b69cf0d664a.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/be4803fec4af9e0009ea0d5a5683e17141a2086812a9df20bfdf976e849cc778.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =b+c\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
